<!-- CHECKPOINT QUIZ -->
<section class="section reveal quiz-ep1">
  <span class="section-num part1-num">CHECKPOINT</span>
  <h2>Probe Your Thinking</h2>
  <p class="quiz-subtitle">No pressure. Just see what stuck.</p>

  <div class="quiz-grid">

  <!-- Q1 -->
  <div class="quiz-card">
    <div class="quiz-card-header">
      <span class="quiz-q-num">Q 01</span>
    </div>
    <p class="quiz-question">When you run <code>fastapi dev main.py</code>, which process is actually listening on port 8000?</p>
    <ul class="quiz-options">
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">A</span>FastAPI directly</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">B</span>Gunicorn</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" data-correct="true" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">C</span>Uvicorn</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">D</span>Python's built-in http.server</button></li>
    </ul>
    <button class="quiz-reveal-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Show Answer <span class="quiz-chevron">▾</span></button>
    <div class="quiz-answer">
      <div class="quiz-answer-inner">
        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(C) Uvicorn</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text"><code>fastapi dev</code> is a convenience wrapper that secretly runs <code>uvicorn main:app --reload</code>. FastAPI is an application framework with no networking capability — Uvicorn is the server that owns the port.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Q2 -->
  <div class="quiz-card">
    <div class="quiz-card-header">
      <span class="quiz-q-num">Q 02</span>
    </div>
    <p class="quiz-question">A request arrives from a browser. In production, put these layers in the correct order it passes through:</p>
    <ul class="quiz-options">
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">A</span>Client → FastAPI → Uvicorn → Gunicorn → Your Function</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" data-correct="true" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">B</span>Client → Gunicorn → Uvicorn → FastAPI → Your Function</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">C</span>Client → Uvicorn → Gunicorn → FastAPI → Your Function</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">D</span>Client → Gunicorn → FastAPI → Uvicorn → Your Function</button></li>
    </ul>
    <button class="quiz-reveal-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Show Answer <span class="quiz-chevron">▾</span></button>
    <div class="quiz-answer">
      <div class="quiz-answer-inner">
        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(B) Client → Gunicorn → Uvicorn → FastAPI → Your Function</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text">Each layer has one job and passes the request inward.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Q3 -->
  <div class="quiz-card">
    <div class="quiz-card-header">
      <span class="quiz-q-num">Q 03</span>
    </div>
    <p class="quiz-question">FastAPI directly handles TCP connections and reads raw bytes from the network.</p>
    <ul class="quiz-options">
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">A</span>True</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" data-correct="true" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">B</span>False</button></li>
    </ul>
    <button class="quiz-reveal-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Show Answer <span class="quiz-chevron">▾</span></button>
    <div class="quiz-answer">
      <div class="quiz-answer-inner">
        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(B) False</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text">FastAPI never touches the network. Uvicorn handles TCP connections, parses HTTP, and passes structured data to FastAPI via the ASGI interface.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Q4 -->
  <div class="quiz-card">
    <div class="quiz-card-header">
      <span class="quiz-q-num">Q 04</span>
    </div>
    <p class="quiz-question">What are the three arguments in the ASGI interface that Uvicorn passes to FastAPI?</p>
    <ul class="quiz-options">
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">A</span>request, response, next</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" data-correct="true" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">B</span>scope, receive, send</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">C</span>method, path, body</button></li>
      <li><button class="quiz-option" type="button"><span class="quiz-opt-letter">D</span>host, port, handler</button></li>
    </ul>
    <button class="quiz-reveal-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Show Answer <span class="quiz-chevron">▾</span></button>
    <div class="quiz-answer">
      <div class="quiz-answer-inner">
        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(B) scope, receive, send</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text"><code>scope</code> contains request metadata (method, path, headers), <code>receive</code> is an async callable to read the body, and <code>send</code> is an async callable to write the response.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

